    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Chronic low back and pelvic pain after remote spinal and pelvic fractures and spinal surgery, with neuropathic features in the right leg; linked to the documented 1925 injuries: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Post-traumatic osteoarthritis of the right ankle and foot after multiple leg fractures and a foot dislocation: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Right leg weakness, atrophy, and shortening after childhood poliomyelitis; a congenital spinal anomaly has been proposed retrospectively: active, provisional [S]</item><item>Long-term opioid therapy for chronic pain, 60 MME a day at intake: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Vitamin D deficiency: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Medication: continued without change, Oxycodone 10 mg oral tablet, one tablet three times daily as needed for pain [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Oxycodone 5 mg oral tablet, one tablet at bedtime as needed for pain [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Duloxetine 60 mg delayed-release oral capsule, one capsule daily [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Acetaminophen 500 mg oral tablet, two tablets three times daily [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Diclofenac sodium 1% topical gel, 2 g to the right ankle four times daily [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Cholecalciferol (vitamin D3) 2,000 units oral tablet, one tablet daily [S]</item><item>Goal: Improve the PEG score by at least 30% from baseline. Outcome by 2026-10-29: PEG fell from 7.3 to 5.3 by the six-week review, a 27% improvement; goal continued [S]</item><item>Goal: Stand at the easel for 30 minutes at a time by the six-week review. Outcome by 2026-10-29: Stands 25 to 30 minutes at the easel with the shoe lift [S]</item><item>Goal: First opioid dose reduction, agreed by the patient, without loss of function. Outcome by 2026-10-29: Reduced from 60 to 52.5 MME a day at the four-week visit; PEG and standing tolerance improved at the six-week review [S]</item><item>Goal: Naloxone in the home with a family member trained to use it. Outcome by 2026-09-17: Naloxone nasal spray dispensed; spouse taught at the first visit [S]</item><item>Continue the care plan agreed on 2026-09-17 [S]</item><item>Scheduled episode complete. Continue routine follow-up [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
